lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.5.dev5.official [64b09905c], v4.5.beta1.official [46c495ca2], v4.5.beta2.official [e1b4101e3]\n- Not reproducible in: v4.5.dev4.official [209a446e3]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev5 - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 09 May 2025 10:53:27 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce GT 520M (nvidia; 390.157) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-2450M CPU @ 2.50GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the camera gets to its limit on the right side for example when it's following the player, it gets jittery until the player stops. It doesn't happen on the left side though. On that side it's working correctly.\nWhat I expect is for the camera to follow the player and when it hits its limit it should stop, the way it did on previous versions.\n\n_A workaround to fix this issue could be:_\n**It must be noted that when you enable the `limit_smoothed` property in the `limit` section of the camera this problem goes away.**\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60593d53-6149-4802-9c0a-44891e6b54d3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Make a camera follow the player (either add it as a child to the player or programmatically make it follow the player)\n- Change the right side limit for the camera to something that you can hit ( 208 for example)\n- Run the scene and move the player to camera's limit on the right side\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Archive.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20744602/Archive.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/